<title>USA: NY business loans down $392 mln in Nov 20 week.</title>
<headline>NY business loans down $392 mln in Nov 20 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $392 billion to $41.911 billion in the week ended Nov 20, Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $392 billion to $42.173 billion.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $11.273 billion to $762.670 billion.</p>
<p>--N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
